   "flags": {},
   "order": 6,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "READ ME",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Keyref for H3 FaceRefine Plus (Qwen Image 2.1 edit)\n\nThe **keyref** is one frame of the shot you want to refine, with the face redrawn sharp and detailed, same pose, expression and light. H3 Face Refine Plus gets it as a reference picture, so it knows what the face should look like *in this shot*.\n\n**Inputs** (examples in `assets/`; copy that folder to `ComfyUI/input/h3plus_example/`):\n- `keyref_source.png` - a crop of one frame of the shot to refine.\n- `keyref_identity_closeup.png` - a crop of the same person in a **close-up of the same clip** (sharp, large face).\n\n**Output:** `keyref_qwen.png`-like image in `output/H3FaceRefinePlus/`. Use it as the keyref picture in the FaceRefine Plus workflow.\n\nMake 2-4 seeds and keep the one that looks most like the person (and least like a different actor). 25 steps at 1024x1024: about 30-60 s on an RTX 5090.\n\nUse Qwen Image Edit, not Flux Kontext / Klein-type editors: in our tests those changed the face into a different person."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "# Keyref for H3 FaceRefine Plus (Qwen Image 2.1 edit)\n\nThe **keyref** is one frame of the shot you want to refine, with the face redrawn sharp and detailed, same pose, expression and light. H3 Face Refine Plus gets it as a reference picture, so it knows what the face should look like *in this shot*.\n\n**Inputs** (examples in `assets/`; copy that folder to `ComfyUI/input/h3plus_example/`):\n- `keyref_source.png` - a crop of one frame of the shot to refine.\n- `keyref_identity_closeup.png` - a crop of the same person in a **close-up of the same clip** (sharp, large face).\n\n**Output:** `keyref_qwen.png`-like image in `output/H3FaceRefinePlus/`. Use it as the keyref picture in the FaceRefine Plus workflow.\n\nMake 2-4 seeds and keep the one that looks most like the person (and least like a different actor). 25 steps at 1024x1024: about 30-60 s on an RTX 5090.\n\nUse Qwen Image Edit, not Flux Kontext / Klein-type editors: in our tests those changed the face into a different person."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 104,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    10,
    40
   ],
   "size": [
    440,
    330
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 7,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Note: 1 - Source frame + identity",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 1 - Source frame + identity\n\n**image 1 - keyref_source:** pick a frame of the shot where the face is clear and typical (not mid-blink, not turned away). Crop a square around the head, about 2x the face size, and save it as PNG. Any image editor works.\n\nIt is scaled to 1024x1024 here: the small, soft face becomes the canvas Qwen redraws.\n\n**image 2 - identity:** a crop of the same person from a **close-up of the same clip**. The refined shot then matches the clip's close-ups (identity vs close-ups 0.74 -> 0.78 in our tests). A generic face reference photo works too, but the result looks less like the clip."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## 1 - Source frame + identity\n\n**image 1 - keyref_source:** pick a frame of the shot where the face is clear and typical (not mid-blink, not turned away). Crop a square around the head, about 2x the face size, and save it as PNG. Any image editor works.\n\nIt is scaled to 1024x1024 here: the small, soft face becomes the canvas Qwen redraws.\n\n**image 2 - identity:** a crop of the same person from a **close-up of the same clip**. The refined shot then matches the clip's close-ups (identity vs close-ups 0.74 -> 0.78 in our tests). A generic face reference photo works too, but the result looks less like the clip."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
